  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Door Sticker",
    "overview": "Every recall is a food-inspection door sticker, the severity scale a Dane already reads at a glance. The level lives in one object: a full-width verdict band across the top of a framed sticker, holding the level's own shape icon and its Danish words, filled by level. The sticker sits on a mint-tinted ground. A graphite-green bar holds two pill nav items, led by a ring-and-dot brand mark. Ink (`#10201a`) is the only brand fill; there is no brand hue to compete with a warning. The reader is one household member on an Android phone, in a kitchen or from a lock-screen push, deciding in seconds whether they have the product. Reading order is verdict band, then product name beside a large photo, then a \"what to do\" strip, then store and date. The system is flat: depth comes from frames and tonal steps, never from shadows. Type is the system font stack only, with sentence-case verdicts and product names at weight 800.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One full-width verdict band per sticker: shape icon plus words, solid only for the levels that can hurt (health red, allergy and possible orange).",
      "2px ink frame on every sticker; the health sticker takes a 3px red frame on a red tint ground.",
      "Product name (22px, 800) and a 96px photo come first under the band; a missing photo shows a package-icon tile.",
      "Ink is the only brand fill: primary button, selected chip, relevance seal.",
      "Flat slabs for controls with an ink edge; pressed sinks 1px.",
      "Light and dark both mint-tinted, never plain gray."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Red Is Health Rule",
        "body": "Red appears only for the `health` level: its band, frame, tint, and the \"bad\" pack-check result. It is never brand, hover, selection, or decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Is The Brand Rule",
        "body": "The only brand fill is ink. Primary button, selected chip and relevance seal are ink; there is no brand hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Shape Beside The Words Rule",
        "body": "Every level has its own shape icon and its own Danish verdict in the band; colour is never the only signal.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Solid Only When It Can Hurt Rule",
        "body": "A band is a solid fill only for health, allergy and possible; the calmer levels use a tint with a level-coloured glyph and text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Relevance Is Black Rule",
        "body": "\"This concerns you\" is a black ink seal (`.badge-mine`); it never recolours the severity.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tokens Only Rule",
        "body": "Font sizes come from `--fs-*` / `--lh-*` in rem; no literal sizes. Dates and `dd` use tabular numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence-Case Verdict Rule",
        "body": "The verdict is sentence case at weight 800; there are no uppercase kickers or eyebrows.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Slab Rule",
        "body": "Controls are flat slabs with an ink edge. Hover tints, pressed sinks, focus is the blue ring. No shadows, no gradients.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** open every sticker with a verdict band that pairs the level's own shape with its Danish words, in sentence case.",
      "**Do** keep text at 4.5:1 and control edges, focus rings and band glyphs at 3:1 in both themes; `test/contrast.test.js` reads the tokens from `styles.css`. Add a pair there when you add a colour token.",
      "**Do** keep voice short and plain: Danish first, English second, imperative.",
      "**Do** keep buttons, inputs and nav targets at 48px; chips 36px with a 48px hit area, 12px between rows.",
      "**Do** gate hover with `@media (hover: hover)` and style `:active` for all input methods.",
      "**Do** show relevance with the black seal.",
      "**Do** give a recall without a usable photo the package-icon tile, never an empty gap."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use red for anything but the health level: not hover, selection or brand.",
      "**Don't** use colour as the only signal of a level.",
      "**Don't** add shadows, gradients or underlines on nav.",
      "**Don't** introduce a brand hue; ink is the only brand fill.",
      "**Don't** write font sizes as literals.",
      "**Don't** let the pack check read \"no match\" as safe on health, allergy, possible or unstated."
    ]
